INT. GALLERIA MALL - SMALL CLAIMS COURT - DAY

A converted shoe store. Rows of benches. A judge's bench where the cash register used to be. The shoe-sizing stool is the witness stand.

JUDGE FELICITY ADEBAYO-STONE, 60s, robe over a cardigan, glasses on a beaded chain. DOMINIC TREMBLAY, 40s, plaintiff, folder of receipts. PETRA LINDGREN, 30s, defendant, flour on her jacket.

JUDGE
(to the room)
Order, order. For the record, this is case 41-C. Mr. Tremblay v. Ms. Lindgren. Mr. Tremblay.

DOMINIC
Your Honor, Ms. Lindgren sold me a wedding cake. It collapsed in the middle of the reception.

JUDGE
Ms. Lindgren?

PETRA
Your Honor, the cake did not collapse. It was pushed.

DOMINIC
By whom?

PETRA
By your uncle.

DOMINIC
My uncle was nowhere near the cake.

PETRA
He was on top of the cake.

JUDGE
Counsel, please.

DOMINIC
I'm not counsel, Your Honor. I'm the groom.

JUDGE
And I'm sorry for your loss, Mr. Tremblay.

DOMINIC
Thank you, Your Honor.

JUDGE
Ms. Lindgren, did the cake have internal supports?

PETRA
Four dowels and a central column.

JUDGE
And your professional opinion on the collapse?

PETRA
Your Honor, nothing in the dowel schedule accounts for a man in a rented tuxedo using the top tier as a diving board.

DOMINIC
That is slander.

PETRA
It is video.

JUDGE
There is video?

PETRA
Eleven phones, Your Honor. I have a flash drive.

JUDGE
(muttering)
Dear God, a flash drive.

DOMINIC
Your Honor, my uncle has a bad knee.

JUDGE
Then he should not have been diving.

PETRA
I rest my case.

DOMINIC
Your Honor, I request a refund of four hundred dollars.

JUDGE
Mr. Tremblay, I request that you never again describe your uncle as "nowhere near" anything.

DOMINIC
Understood.

JUDGE
Judgment for the defendant. Ms. Lindgren, you may keep the cake.

PETRA
There is no cake, Your Honor.

JUDGE
Then I recommend you keep the flash drive.

The gavel, a shoehorn, cracks on the register. Dominic gathers his receipts. Petra gathers her jacket. The Judge rubs her temples.
